- 5. Clinical Application & Analysis: {"5-1. clinical_dataset": "UK Biobank", "5-2. diseases_studied": "Pathogenic CNVs (including 1q21.1 distal deletion and duplication, 15q11.2 deletion and duplication, 16p11.2 deletion and duplication, 16p13.11 deletion and duplication)", "5-3. clinical_groups_n": "UKB-IDP-CNV: 263; UKB-CNV (Jacobian): 375. For 1q21.1 deletion: n=5; for 1q21.1 duplication: n=5.", "5-4. clinical_groups_age": "UKB-IDP-CNV: mean 62.97 (sd 8.70), range 46-80; UKB-CNV (Jacobian): mean 63.58 (sd 7.48), range 46-80", "5-5. clinical_groups_sex": "UKB-IDP-CNV: F 54.4%, M 45.6%; UKB-CNV (Jacobian): F 55.4%, M 44.5%", "5-6. deviation_metric": "z-score; count of extreme deviations (|z| > 2)", "5-7. association_analysis": "Spearman correlation between the total count of extreme deviation scores and a general cognitive ability score.", "5-8. key_findings_brief": "The study demonstrates the utility of normative modeling to map individualized brain deviation scores in CNV carriers, revealing a high degree of heterogeneity and a correlation between negative deviations and lower cognitive function.", "5-9. key_findings_detailed": "Structural measures were most informative for CNV-related deviations. The study highlighted 1q21.1 distal deletion and duplication, showing that deletion carriers had more positive deviations (lower brain volume) and duplication carriers had more negative deviations (larger brain volume), consistent with known dosage effects. A significant negative correlation was found between the count of negative deviations and a general cognitive ability score (r = -0.04, P = 0.04).", "5-10. key_limitations": "Lack of longitudinal imaging data, especially in younger participants. The individual deviation scores might be driven by factors other than the CNVs. The reference samples are disproportionately of European ancestry, limiting generalizability.", "5-11. application_notes": "The study proposes an \"individual patient first\" approach, using normative models to create individualized risk profiles that can help understand the impact of pathogenic CNVs at an individual level, moving beyond traditional case-control studies."}
- 6. General Notes: "The study provides a comprehensive framework for applying normative modeling to investigate the effects of rare genetic variants (CNVs) on brain structure and cognition at an individual level. The use of large-scale datasets and the focus on individual differences are key strengths. The authors also provide code for their analyses."
